An analogue signal $S_{I}$ is converted into a digital signal $D$ using an analogue-to-digital converter (ADC). After transmission of the digital signal, it is converted back to an analogue signal $S_{T}$ using a digital-to-analogue converter (DAC), as illustrated in Fig. 5.1.

